    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "San Antonio ist eine traditionsreiche Gemeinde im Corozal-Distrikt, die als eines der Zentren des Zuckerrohranbaus in Belize gilt. Das Dorf ist geprägt von weiten Feldern, die während der Erntesaison in ein geschäftiges Treiben tauchen. Die Bewohner von San Antonio sind stolz auf ihre Identität als Mestizen und pflegen ihre kulturellen Wurzeln durch Sprache, Musik und kulinarische Spezialitäten. Trotz der Dominanz der Zuckerindustrie diversifiziert das Dorf zunehmend seine Landwirtschaft, was zu einer stabilen lokalen Wirtschaft beiträgt. Die geordnete Struktur des Dorfes und die gepflegten öffentlichen Plätze spiegeln den Fleiß und die Organisation der Gemeinschaft wider. San Antonio bietet Besuchern einen authentischen Einblick in das Leben einer prosperierenden Agrargemeinschaft im nördlichen Belize.",
      hu: "San Antonio Corozal District egyik ismertebb falusi k?z?ss?ge, ahol a helyi identit?s, a mez?gazdas?gi k?rnyezet ?s az ?szaki belizei falusi ?let szorosan ?sszekapcsol?dik. A telep?l?s a k?z?ss?gi eml?kezet ?s a mindennapi munka tere, nem pedig egy egyszer? tranzitpont. Az ilyen falvak adj?k Corozal vid?k?nek t?rsadalmi m?lys?g?t, mert itt a csal?d, a t?j ?s a szomsz?ds?g egy?tt m?k?dik. F?ldrajz K7 - k?z?ss?gi falvak ?s mez?gazdas?gi t?jak.",
      ro: "San Antonio este un sat harnic din districtul Corozal, care trăiește în principal din agricultură și este o parte vitală a centurii de zahăr din nord. Comunitatea se caracterizează prin dedicarea sa față de cultivarea trestiei de zahăr, câmpurile înconjurătoare dominând economia și peisajul local. San Antonio are o identitate mestizo puternică, spaniola fiind limba principală vorbită în stradă și în case. Satul este cunoscut pentru spiritul său rezistent și muncitor, precum și pentru atmosfera sa comunitară primitoare. În ciuda concentrării sale pe agricultură, satul are un număr tot mai mare de mici afaceri care deservesc nevoile locuitorilor săi.",
      en: "San Antonio is a hardworking village in the Corozal District that lives primarily from agriculture and is a vital part of the northern sugar belt. The community is characterized by its dedication to sugarcane cultivation, with the surrounding fields dominating the local economy and landscape. San Antonio has a strong Mestizo identity, with Spanish being the primary language spoken in the streets and homes. The village is known for its resilient and industrious spirit, as well as its welcoming community atmosphere. Despite its focus on agriculture, the village has a growing number of small businesses that serve the needs of its residents. For those traveling through the Corozal District, San Antonio provides a genuine look at the rural life that sustains northern Belize. The village remains a proud and prosperous part of the district's network of agricultural communities, where tradition and modern farming go hand in hand."
    },
